{"id":"besagt","lemma":"besagt","pos":"adj","rank":3895,"glosses":["said, aforesaid, implied, mentioned"],"ipa":"/bəˈzaːkt/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3d/De-besagt.ogg/De-besagt.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Was besagt es?","en":"What does it say?","words":[{"g":"what"},null,{"g":"it"}]},{"text":"Was besagt sein Schweigen?","en":"What does his silence imply?","words":[{"g":"what"},null,{"g":"to be"},{"g":"silence"}]},{"text":"Das besagt nicht, dass ich bleiben kann.","en":"That doesn't mean I can stay.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"not"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"to remain"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"}]},{"text":"Das besagt nicht unbedingt, dass du recht hast.","en":"It doesn't necessarily mean that you're right.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"not"},{"g":"absolutely, definitely"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"you"},{"g":"right, right-hand"},{"g":"have","l":"haben"}]},{"text":"Schweigen besagt oft Zustimmung.","en":"Silence often implies consent.","words":[{"g":"silence"},null,{"g":"often"},{"g":"agreement"}]}]}